Comments:
1. Evaluator: Kiana Setoodehnia, September 13, 2024
2. The nuclear Q-value is based on 36Ca mass excess measured by J. Surbrook et al., Phys. Rev. C 103 (2021) 014323.
3. The energies and spin-parities are from N. Dronchi et al., Phys. Rev. C 107, 034306 (2023); T. Beck et al., Phys. Rev. C 108 (2023) L061301; L. Lalanne et al., 
   Phys. Rev. Lett. 129 (2022) 122501; L. Lalanne et al., Phys. Rev. C 101 (2021) 055809; and N. Nica et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 113 (2012) 1.
4. The spectroscopic factors and gamma-ray partial widths for resonances above 1 MeV come from N. Dronchi et al., Phys. Rev. C 107, 034306 (2023). Those gamma-ray
   partial widths are scaled for the new resonance energies.
5. The proton and gamma partial widths of the 448-keV resonance are scaled from those of N. Dronchi et al., Phys. Rev. C 107, 034306 (2023). 
6. The experimental rate agrees with the TALYS rate at 10 GK within the uncertainties. Therefore, no high-temperature rate matching is needed.
